menu "DSP Engine"

config DSP_CHARACTER_PROFILE
    bool "Enable Analog Character per-stage cycle profiling"
    default n
    help
        Enable per-stage cycle-counter instrumentation for Character DSP.
        This adds cycle-counter reads inside the sample loop and is intended
        only for profiling builds. Keep disabled for normal playback.


config DSP_PEQ_USE_ESP_DSP
    bool "Use ESP-DSP stereo block biquad for PEQ"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    default n
    help
        Experimental Phase 3 backend. Converts each PCM block to interleaved
        float, then runs the PEQ cascade with ESP-DSP's stereo biquad kernel.
        This preserves the filter coefficients but uses a DF-II state
        realization instead of the native transposed DF-II implementation.
        Keep disabled for the reference backend. Enable for A/B CPU and
        listening tests before making it the default.

config DSP_PEQ_USE_ESP_DSP_AES3
    bool "Use ESP-DSP dual-mono biquad (ESP32-S3 AES3 eligible)"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3 && !DSP_PEQ_USE_ESP_DSP
    default n
    help
        Experimental A/B backend. Deinterleaves PCM into two planar float
        channels and calls dsps_biquad_f32 for each channel. With a recent
        ESP-DSP package and optimized kernels enabled, the S3-specific
        dsps_biquad_f32_aes3 assembly can be selected. Otherwise the library
        falls back to another available implementation. Keep disabled until
        measured against the native and interleaved-stereo backends.

endmenu
